      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <head>DIARRHCEA.</head>
        <p>DIARRHCEA.</p>
        <p>During the last half-century every- one travelling in hot climes has made a point of carrying some DR. J. COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLORODYNE,</p>
        <p>so as to stop immediately an attack of</p>
        <p>DIARRHCEA,</p>
        <p>DYSENTERY OR CHOLERA</p>
        <p>Hot weather in the British Isles strikes suddenly, and everyone should take a little precaution. Don't wait till you actually need the Cblorodyne, but always keep it by you. Avoid disappointment and insist on having DR' J. COLLIS BROWNE'S</p>
        <p>CHLORODYNE.</p>
        <p>IT ACTS LIKE A CHARM.</p>
        <p>Of all Chemists, is. lid., 2s. 9d. and 4s. Gd.</p>
