        <head>INSIDE EXHIBITS.</head>
        <p>INSIDE EXHIBITS.</p>
        <p>Window plants (for members with no greenhouse.— Geranium: 1, J. Jackson; 29 Mrs. Caldwell ; 3, S. A. Drinkwater. Fuschia : 1, George Tomlin; 2' H. Fletcher; 3, S. A. Drinkwater. Aspidistra : 1, Mrs. Wood; 2, Harry Lawrence; 3, H. Fletcher; he, G. F. Rice; 3, Mrs. Griffiths. Campanula : 1, Mrs. Hatton; 2, H. Harrop. Castor oil plant: 1, 11. Harrop ; 2, H. Lawrence; 3,41. Ellieon. Palm: Miss Hilda Sergeant Begonia: I, H. Harrop; 2, S. A. Drinkwater. Foliage plant: George Tomlin. Plant in flower: Jackson. Window-box.-1, H. Lawrence; special, G. Sanders. Hanging Basket.-1, Mrs. D. Hill; 2, George Sanders. Plan!s (may to greenhonse grown).—Geranitires : T. Ellison. Fuchsias: G. ainders. Ferns : Mrs. E. J. Daintith. Foliage plants (any variety) : Mrs. S. William. Flowering plants (any variety) • F. H. Longshaw. Lill= : 1, Mrs. V. M. Taylor ; '2, George Tomlin. _ - _ _</p>
        <p>Group of plants (open to all members).-1, James Owen; 2, T. Ellison. Cut Flowers.-Asters: I, F., H. Long thaw ; 2, Mrs. E. J. Daintith ; 3, Mrs. Hatton; h c, J. Jackson; c, H. Harrop. Pansies: 1, H. Harrop; 2. J. Jackson; 3, J. D. Goodliffe (spec,al, merit). Violas On not bass than three varieties): H. Harrop. Collection of four distinct varieties of cut bloom: 1, F. H. Longshaw ; 2, Charles Plinston ; 3, H. Harrop. Collection of four varietie3, cut flowers, out-door grown : I, Mrs. D. Hill ; 2 George Tomlin ; 3, Mrs. Hatton; h c, H. Harrop; c, J. Jackson. Vase: 1, H. Harrop ; 2, Mrs, Hatton ; 3, J. Jackson. Cut Flowers (open classes).-Six dahlias: 1, James Owen; 2, A. J. Moltram ; 3, D. Bonehill. Violas (in not less than three varieties) : • 1, D. Bonehill ; 2, A. J. Mottram ; 3, James Owen. Sweet peas: I, Peter Cliffe ; 2, James Owen; 3, Charles Plinston ; h c, A. J. Mottram ; c, D. Bonehill. Roses (any variety) : 1, Richard Daintith ; 2, A. J. Mottram; 3, James Owen ; h c, R. H. Daintith. Vase of flowers: 1, E. Daintith; 2, James Owen; 3, H. Tomlin. Collectiorrof cut blooms (four varieties): 1, Israel Hampson ; 2. James Owen.; 3, A. J. Mottrarn ; h c. D. Bonebill ; e' H. Tomlin. School Children's Classes.-Hand bouquet of wild flowers: 2 and medal, Phylis Burrows, Bolton Council ' School; 2. Ellen Garnett, Bolton Council School; 3, Frank Drinkwater, Heathside ; 4, Elsie Whitfield, Arpley-street ; h c, Emma Gifford, Bolton Council School. Fuchsia, grown in greenhouse or frame: 2, Frank Thomas, Beamont School; I, Hilda Sergeant, Fairfield; 3, John Fairhurst, Latchford St. Mary's. Fuchsia (not grown in greenhouse) : 1, and medal, Florence Bond, St. Barnabas' ; 2, Thomas Owen, Silver-street; 3, William Beswick, St. Barnabss; 4, Eva Bristow, Heatbside ; h c, Annie Hitchmough, Arpley-street ' • c, Stanley Hill and Albert Potter, Parochial. Geranium, grown- in greenhouse or frame: 1 and medal, Edward Bate., Christ Church; 2, Florence Whittingbam, Arpley-street •, 3, Harold Brownian], Hamilton-street; 4, Leonard Johnson, St. James'; h c, Nellie Egerton, St. Ann's; c, Dorothy Bennett and Vera Clarke, Arpley-street, and Edward Sykes, Christ Church. Plessed flowers or leaves; 1 and medal, Rhoda Grant, St. James'; 2, Emily Johnson, St. James';</p>
        <p>3, Percy Hill, Heathsid., ; 4, Stanley Hill, Parochial_ ; h c, Zelia Siddall, St. Barnabls'.</p>
        <p>THE SCHOOLS.</p>
        <p>A competition was held in the various schools an] the results is a 4 follows : _ _ _</p>
        <p>_ Holy Trinity : 1, Gilbert G. Titahard ;2, Beatrice Killion; 3, Joseph Titchard. Arpley-street : 1, C. Cross; 2, Amy Bowcoek '• 3. F. Whittiqgham. St. Barnabas : 1, Floreace Bond and William Beswick ;2, Elizabeth Green ;3, John Boozli and Emily Gleave. Sacred Heart : 1, Fred Buckles ;2, Thomas Moran '• 3, Thomas Flat,nagen. Latchford St. James: 1, Lily Butterworth ; 2, Leonard Johnson ; 3, Herbert Foster. Latchford St. Mary's: 1, John Fair- hurst ; 2, Tnoinas Taylor; 3, Georga Proctor. Latchford Christ Church : 1, Edward Sykes ; 2, Edward Bite; 3, John Ward, Latchford Bolton School: 1, Dorothy Millard and Elsie Blease ; 2, Beatrice Marshall and Doris Bradbui ; 3, Emma "Gifford and Phyllis Barrow, St. Alban's : 1, Frank Appleton ;2, Mary 0' Bi ten ;3, May McCormack. Heathside boys': 1, Elio Kindon ; Frank Hinchcliffe and Ernest Hughes; 3, Frank Dzipkwater and Charlie Lee. Heathside girls': 1, Doris Holbrook : 2, Mary Dickenson; 3, R. Walton. Wycliffe : I, Frat.le Rowlance ; 2, Alice Smith; 3, Madge Stephens. St. Ann's : Geranium' 1, Nellie Egerton; 2, Reginald Dykes ; 3, James Cunnington. and William Forter ' • and fuchsia, 1, Mary Carroll; 2 Reginald Johnson; 3, Willie Dykes and James Clare. gilver-street : 1, Thomas Owen ; 2, Hilda Fletcher ; 3, J. Meakin and Fred Rowe. Sr. Benedict's, Orford-lane: 1, M. Wisedale ; 2, T. Farrell ; 3, Fiancis Da,gnall. Hamilton-street boys : Geranium. 1, Sam Hackott ; 2, Harold Brownbill and Thomas Ayres; 3, George Hollingworth ad Harry Glover; and fuchsias, 1, William Astley ; 2, Albert Poi ter : 3, James Lomax. Hamilton-street girls' : 1, Jessie Holbrook ; 2, Dorothy Wilkinson ;3, Lily Titley. St. Mary's boys : I, W. 11 Newlin ; 2,Frank O'Toole ; 3,Herbert Ashton. St. Mary's girls: 1, Florrie Ball; 2, Ellen Thompson;3, Mary Stirrup. Smith-street : I, Minnie Jolley ; 2, Sarah Lomax ; 3 Edith Tomkinsrn. Parochial : Geraniums' 1, James ' Shepley • 2, Walter Challenor ; 3, Harry Challenor • and fuchsia, 1, Albert Gotter ; 2, Stanley Hill ; Walt:r Harold Holden. Fairfield girls' : 1. Mary Ferguson; 2, Doris Thompson; 3, E. King. Fairfield uporr girls' : 1, Lillie Weston ; 2, Ethel Lightfoot ; 3, Ella Cotton. Bcamont girls': 1, Mabel Pilkington ; 2, Mallon South; 3, Doris Taylor and Lily Monoss. Beamont boys': 1,-S. Ogden; 2, W. Vincent and F. Altman ; 3, E. Daniels and F. Rawlinson.</p>
