      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0026" n="art0026">
        <head>NOTES BY " OVALIST."</head>
        <p>NOTES BY " OVALIST."</p>
        <p>191 t fail to study the particulars of our football • oto . a _prize scheme announced on this page. There vouple of crowns waiting to be picked up by 4''vtators at Wilderspool to-day. -- 1•4:111e curtain rises on another season at 3.30. War- ihar°,ll's faithful supporters will note with pleasure of tattle trouble spent on the turf has been productive Lets "li good, and the-. playing pitch never looked c);!r than it does to-day. Improvements on the are in contemplation, and if more accommoda- d a better stand can be provided on the mem- gire„ flio a good deal will have been achieved in the 'tlou of making the enclosure first-clas3. 114 e, tringtonians are entering upon the season with qati‘ confidence, and there has been little left to Yek.ce in the way of preparation. The lesson of a talte a,go has not been forgotten, and the thirteen who "the ft"e field to-day will be fit, fresh and eager for \viti,ray- I don't think much of Leigh's chance, not- the optimism which has been exuding ~ather-lane for weeks past. The odds are 2to Wirepullers, and if Leigh haven't a twq- Itit„e. raargin against them at a p.m. I shall be vrised.</p>
