      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>Cricket.</head>
        <p>Cricket.</p>
        <p>Having concluded their League programme and annexed the League honours, Warrington engaged in a friendly match with Wigan on Saturday. This was the return engagement and, like the first meeting, it resulted in a draw. Wigan had first turn at the wicket end, and, thanks chiefly to a good display by A. Jones who made 49, they amassed 132. Warrington had responded with 98 for the loss of 6 wickets when play ceased. W. Richardson was in great form and after batting for an hour and a half he carried out his bat with 48 to his credit.</p>
        <p>Warrington 2nd suffered defeat at Wigan by the nairow. margin of six runs. The visitors' total of 07 included creditable displays by NV. V. Turton and W. Houghton who knockesl up 34 and 17 respectively. Wigan replied with 73, J. Healey ling the top scorer with 23. D. Plinston bowled very effectively, captur- ing seven wickets for .28 runs.</p>
        <p>Rylands' had no difficulty in disposing of White- cross Recreation on Saturday, thus gaining the second position' in the Warrington and District League. Whitecross were out for the small total of 13 runs,and Rylands'. secured these without the loss of a wicket. McGowan bowled splendidly and took five wickets for runs, performing the hat trick.</p>
        <p>St. James's tried conclusions wtth Cheshire Lines Engineers and the match ended in a draw in which the saints had the best of matters. The champions com- piled the total of 121 for 7 wickets and the Engineers replied with 88 for the same loss. J. H. Constable distinguished himself with a brilliant not out innings of 55, whilst J. Duckworth also pled fine cricket for 41, Hallam took five wickets for 23 runs.</p>
        <p>Walker's Brewery inflicted a severe trouncing on Wilderspool Brewery, the respective totals being 104 and 28. W. Rylance wielded the willow in splendid style, placing 51 to his credit. Spicer captured five wickets for eight rims.</p>
        <p>Walker's Brewery are to he congratulated upon winning the championship of the Manchester and District Brewery League. Their record in this tourney is :—Played 12, won 10, lost 2.</p>
        <p>Sankey Wire Mills suffered a reverse at the hands of the" Guardian " office, the feature of the match being a brilliant innings by Levi Riley who made 75 in faultless style. Paton captured six wickets for 16 runs.</p>
        <p>Sankey have gained the championship of the Warrington and District Junior League for the second year in succession. On Saturday they vanquished Orford by a majority of 30. Forster took four wickets for eight runs and Webb five for ten.</p>
        <p>Lymm registered a victory at the expense of Liverpool Strollers, T. Marsh shining in both the batting and bowling departments. He knocked up 34 and took six wickets for 14 runs. Rouse captured four for 27.</p>
        <p>Oughtrington Park triumphed over Bowdon second, N. Ward being the most successful batsman with 71,</p>
