      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>MONKS, HALL AND CO 'S RECREATION CLUB.</head>
        <p>MONKS, HALL AND CO 'S RECREATION CLUB.</p>
        <p>Annual Gala.</p>
        <p>• A pleasant afternoon favoured the annual gala pro- moted by the recreation club in connection with Messrs Morks, Hall and Co., Ltd. which was held on the recreation ground, Lovely-lane, on SAturday. The club mtinues to make good progress and the gala was adrnitably organized and proved very successful. The first it3m of the programme was the ope,ning of the new air tifle shooting range by Captain Owen who expressed his pleasure thckt the rising generation was taking more interest in military matters. He 'fired the fit short and obtained a" bull's eye." Considerable amrsement, was created by a novelty cricket match h3tween Mr. Owen's team and Mr. Morris's team. The prize for the best costume was awarded to George Shaw, who was in ladies' attire.</p>
        <p>The flower shjow was a decided improvement ppon lest year's and an open class attracted some excellent entrier. A pretty collection of cut flowers sent for exhibition by %Ira. Hall attracted general admiration. Mr. F. W. Monks IR opening the show said he was glad to hear that the affairs of the club had been carried on so successfully by the committee, and the directors were cordially in favour of the movement. He w sorry that, owing to bad trade, they Ind not been able to do as much as they would like, but they hoped to do better in future. (Applsuse). A hearty vote"of thanks was passed to Mr. Monks for opening the show, on the motion of Mr. G. Bowman. During the afternoon sports were held and the Penketh Tannery Prize Band playel selections. In the evening there was dancing. The arrangements were well carried out by the following officials :—Honorary president Alderman T. Burton; president, Mr. G. Bcro man ; vice-presidents, Messrs. F. R. Monks, A. .1. Monks. D. Ikin, B. Deakin, J. E. Washington, S. Baxter, W. Murray, J. Burthem, D. Bill, A. Millar, F. A. Rathbone, R. Pemberton, E. Winter, G. Higgs, M. B. Lewis, A. Oakley, H. Burthem and T. Morgan ; general committee (forge), Messrs. J. Cortadine, W. Boyle A. Adams, J. Booth, E. Powell, and A. Thßmas, (tube) Messrs. R. Done, W. Nightingale, and J. Barrett, (bedsteads) Messrs. G. Clare and W. Talbot (rivet) Messrs. G. Shaw and Wm. Webb ; cricket com- mittee, Messrs. C. Davey, R. Done, A. Smith, J. Smith, G. Cox, H. Lindley, G. Show, J. Booth, and E. Powell; bowling committee, Messrs. J. Timminr, J. Cox, J. Thomason, James Shaw, B. Webe, P. Walsh, P. Gleave, W. Nightingale, F. Barlow, and J. Barrett; hon. treasurer, Mr. S. Sisson ; hon. auditors, Messrs. C. Davey and R. D. Owen ; secretary, Mr. .1. Webb ; flower show committee, Messrs. G. Richards, W. Talbot, H. Hickling, J. Turner, E. Hill, J. Woolley, R. Cleave, and C. Llewellyn ; hon. secrettu y to the flower show, Mr. G. W. Clare; judges for the flower show, Messrs. Howard and Parker; fudges for the sports. Messrs. J. T. Smith, NV. Taylor, W. C. Litten and F. Fieldhowe ; starter, Mr. J. Harvey : handicappers and stewards, the committee.</p>
        <p>The following were the prize-winners at the flower show :</p>
