        <p>THE EXAMINER• Series OF WEEK-END NEWSPAPERS COMPRISES:-</p>
        <p>THE WARRINGTON EXAMINER published every Saturday morning. The principal and the oldest weekly paper for War- rington, Stockton Heath, Penketh, Winwick, Padgate Lymm, Scc., being one of the largest and best weekly papers in Lancashire and Cheshire. The district covered by this paper comprises a large trading and agricultural tract in South Lancashire and Mid- Cheshire.</p>
        <p>RUNCORN EXAMINER, published every 1 Saturday morning. It is the best weekly paper in rown and district, and offers the best and cheapest facilities to advertisers.</p>
        <p>THE WIDNES EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. Widnes' contains the largest number of chemical works of any town in the Kingdom, and is a rapidly growing centre of industry.</p>
        <p>- - THE EARLESTOWN AND NEWTON EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. The largest local paper containing the news of Earlestown, Newton-le-Willows, Go!borne, Haydock, Lowton, kcc The district thus comprised is a most important part of the Lancashire coalfields. rPHE ST. HELENS EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning, circulating in St. Helens, Prescot, Parr, Sutton, Peasley Cross, &amp;c.—the centre of the glass, chemical and watch trades of thd Kingdom.</p>
