      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0066" n="art0066">
        <head>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL.</p>
        <p>TLe monthly meting of the lure' District Council was held on Wednesday afternoon in Bewsey Cblll3l 3rs. Mr. R. Forshaw preside i and others nresent were : Messrs J. BacPhonse, W. Mather, W. F urners J. Ball, W. Houghton, A. Brooks, .1. C. Sutton (clerk), B. S. Newcombe (surueyor), 11. P. Borrige (arTistsnt surveyor), F. W. liei root (nspector). Mr. HOUGHTON referring to the question of Spittal Bridge ram aing to the Ces it -nen raid: "I want to modify or, sty sometb:ng you slid at the lest meeting. It is hardly justico to Mr. Mather and myself when you stated at the last meeting. 'I have reason to believe that the demsnds of the owners were not exorbitant They were terms which would lead to a settlement '?ls that c irrectly reported ?" The CHAI R3l AN : Yes. It is ! . .</p>
        <p>Hocoirrox. : Don't you think it is exorbitant ? The CHAIRMAN: Don't you think you should have mentioned that at the last meeting? I cannot allow you to go on with this. Mr. HOUGHTON said he wonld obey Hs ruling, but be objected to it. No businecs of public interest was discusEe3.</p>
