      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0070" n="art0070">
        <head>' AN AMERICAN , FLYER.</head>
        <p>' AN AMERICAN , FLYER.</p>
        <p>Mr. H. Glen Curtiss, America's sole repre- sentative at Rheims, distinguished himself by Winning the Gordon Bennett International 'Cup and £l,OOO. In the speed contest he beat all records by flying at the rate Of 48 miles an hour. The International Cup, having gone to the United States, will now have to be fought for next year in America, 4</p>
