        <head>Cadishead</head>
        <p>Cadishead</p>
        <p>„ /3ACRING THE BUDGEL—On Saturday evening an "Ithusiastic open-air meeting in support of the Budget 144 s held near the Jubilee lamp, Cadishead. Mr. F. all presided over a large gathering and the speaker :as Councillor Middleton of Oldham. A resolution uPP°rting the Budget was unanimorsly carried. Winwick. (MAR DROWNING FATALITY.--Mr. Brighouse w an inquest at the Swan Hotel, Winwick, on e e'leziday, relative to the death of Harold Hatch, aged v,eyenteen, of 39, Fothergill-street, Warrington. ',whose was found in the St. Helens and Widnes Canal, at suljt`vick, on Sunday. It was stated that deceased th .ered from epileptic fits. He was seen walking along r e canal bank onl Sunday, %%hen he suddenly twisted ,oend and fell into the canal.—A verdict of ” Acci- f,lltal death" was returned, due to fulling in the water "en seized with a fit. Stretton .LACCIDENT.—A cyclist named Mr. Frank Ball, residing Tanners•row Houses, Stretton, met with a somewhat rriolis accident on Saturday evening. He was riding Y :gr.. J. Ellison's shop and, having no light and T,g slightly c'eaf, dashed into a cart belonging to Mr. in' 'haw, butcher, Stockton Heath,which was approach- The driver immed'ltely pulled up and went to assistance. He found him to be suffering from iNuries to the head and face, and on being conveyed iTrae he was attended to by Dr. Bower, who ordered la.removal to the Werrington Infirmary where he is 411113-patient.</p>
