      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-04_WidnesExaminer_art0122" n="art0122">
        <head>LIST OF PRESENTS.</head>
        <p>LIST OF PRESENTS.</p>
        <p>Bridegroom to Bride, pearl necklace and gold keeper ring .</p>
        <p>Ifride to Bridegroom, oak desk Bridegroom to Bridesmaids, turquoise pendants Father of Bride, piano and cheque Mother of Bride, Household and table linen Mother of Bridegroom, cheque Mr. and Mrs. John Dodds, dinner service Mr. and Mrs. E 4 V. Walker, case of cutlery and silver Miss Marjcrie Dodds, dessert spoons Mr. P. L. Dads' silver cake knife Mr. J. Hepple Dodds, works of Dickens Mr. M. F'. Dodds, table spoons Messrs. and Miss Walker, silver Queen Anne tea service Mrs. Alderley, silver candlesticks and inkstand Miss Alderley, crocheted tea cloth Mrs. Baker, brass spirit kettle and stand Mrs. W. H. and Miss Dodds (Newcastle-on-Tyne) silver rose bowl Mrs. and the Misses Dodds (Durham), afternoon tea cloth Messrs. W. and H. Dodds, pair of pictures Mr. and Mrs. Kenyon, beaten brass ornament Mrs. the Misses and Dr. J. Dodds Marshall, silver vases Miss Ethel and Dr. W. P. Marshal, silver clock Mrs. Stockdale, tea cosy Miss Stockdale, lustre vase Miss Doris Stockdale, drawn thread nightdress case Mr. E. E. Abrahamson, black and copper flower stand Mr. and Mrs. Airey end family, mahogany chiming clock Mr. and Mrs. J. B. Aitken, case of silver teaspoons and sugar tongs. Mr. and Mrs. Ambler, copper hot water jug Mr. and Mrs. Appleton, silver and cut glass butter dish In case Miss Bailey, embroidered satin pincushion Rev. J. Agar Beet, D.D. and Mrs. Beet, Venetian vase Mr. Beswick, brushes, etc. Mr. and Mrs. Billing (Shrewsbury), silver card case Mr. and Mrs. C. H. Bindloss, silver ihkstand Miss Bindloss, tea service Mr. and Mrs. H. S. Bleckly, silver mirror Mr. J. R. Blytb, silver photo frame Miss Booth, set of d'oyleys Mrs. Budden, flower vase Dr. and Mrs. Buchan, silver cake stand Mr. Robert Cameron,M.P. and Mrs. Cameron, palm pot Mrs. Colin Cooke, salad servers Mrs. Coop, duchesse set</p>
        <p>Dr.and M:is.Crookwell &amp; family, pewter hot water jug Mr. A. H. Crosfield, M.P. and Mrs. Crosfield, gold and jade necklace Mr. and Mrs. F. J. Crossfield (Todbusk Park, trlverston), silver entree dish Mr. and Mrs. P. Davies, scales and weights Mr. and Mrs. W. Davies, case of fish knives and forks Mr. John Davies, tea pot Miss Bessie Dutton, plant pot Messrs. J. and W. Dutton, duchesse set Mr. W. R.-Earp, Macaulay's Works Mr. Edwards, chafing dish Messrs. Eustance and Co., silver egg frame Mr. and Mrs. Farnworth, silver revolving dish The Misses Farnwortb, silver sugar sifter The Misses Fleldhouse, embroidered cushion cover Mr. R. G. S. Finney, silver calendar Messrs. W. A. and S. Forster, a nest of Sheraton tables The Misses Forster, case of silver nutcrackers and grape scissors Miss Emma Foster, crochet Mr. and Mrs. Gandy, drawn thread tray cloth Mr. and Mrs. David Garnett (Southport), mahogany pedestal</p>
