        <p>BOTELER- GRAMMAR SCHOOL. THE NEXT TERM WILL COMMENCE ON THURSDAY, SEPTEMBER 16th at 9 a.m. The Headmaster will be at the School on the previous day from 11 to 1 and 3t05 to interview parents of new parents of new Boys and others. The school affords a sound Classical or Commercial education. The Honours of the past year include a University Exhibition, Civil Service appointments Scheme, Boy Clerkship, Public Sehool Scholarship, and il6 successes n the recent Oxford Locals. All candidates passed. The Headmaster will be pleased to forward on appli- cation the School Prospectus and supply other informa- tion. VERB B. DAVIES. Law Clerk to the Governors.</p>
        <p>BOTELER GR.A.MMAR SCHOOL.— An EXAMINATION WILL BE HELD at the SCHOOL on Sotardayt September Mb, at 9.30 a.m. for the purpose of electing one Boteler Scholar. Candidates who must have been in attendance at one of the Public Elementary Schools in the County Borough of Warrington during the last three years at least, must be under the age of 12 on the day of the Examination. The subjeets for examination will be Arithmetic, English Grammar, History and Geography. Candidates must send in their names to the Head- master together with a letter testimonial from their present Schools not later than Wednesday, Septem- ber Bth. VERE B. DAVIES, Law Clerk to the Governors. COUNTY ROROUGH OF WARRINGTON. EDUCATION COMMITTEE. ARCHITECTURAL COMPETITION FOR A PUBLIC ELEMENTARY SCHOOL. The above-named are prepared to receive from Architects COMPETITIVE PLANS for the erection of a PUBLIC ELEMENTARY SCHOOL. A copy of the Conditions of Competition and the Instructions to competing Architects, together with a plan of the site, may be obtained on and after Monday, the 6th September, 1909, on payment of £1 is. (which will be returned on the receipt of a bona-fide set of plans), from Education Office, J. MOORE MURRAY, Sankey at., Warrington. Secretary and Director. Ist September, 1909.</p>
