        <p>_ FOOTBALL SEASON OPENS. NORTHERN UNION LEAGUE Leigh Win at Home against York. At Mather-lane on Wednesday, Leigh defeated York bY 11 points to three. York, who had the wind and sun at their backs, were Ileveral times dangerous before Daniells had to retire "with an injury. Davies, of Leigh, got away on the %gin&amp; kicked into the open when pressed by Moore, and alith followed up EO quickly that he scored near the Sts." A grand bit of work by Bolewski and O'Neill taved the way for Davies to record a second try, Sam 'Johnson missing the goal. Leigh crossed over with a clear six points lead, and !ith York short-handed there was not much doubt as to issue. The visitors, however, played up pluckily, Tlci beat Leigh in the scrums, and their efforts were pvarded by Plummer dropping a couple of neat goals. „or the home lot Tom Johnson scored close in and Sam Vrnson obliged with a neat goal, leaving Leigh winners "7 seven points. HULL TOO GOOD FOR BRADFORD. At the Boulevard on Thursday, Hull defeated Brad- lord bylB points to 3. vt,lt was just on half-time when the first points accrued nalton dashing over under the posts for G. Rogers to Pilot a goal. In the end Hull's superior speed and leteral tactics resulted in clever tries to Wallace, daderson and E. Rogers, G. Rogers adding two more goals. Dunbavin scored for Bradford. A THRASHING FOR ST. lIELENS. St. Helens were severely thrashed at Hull on Thum- -31. ageinsttheKingston Rovers to the tune of 39 Po' . 14.8 to 7, and Turtill, New Zealander, found his berth full bick for his new club no sinezure. Turtill jlekked a penalty for tke losers and coverted a try by fson. "ALL BLACK " FOR HUDDERSFIELD. Tile Huddersfield Northern Rugby Union Club have tecUred the signature of W. Trevarthen, one of the ell,et forwards who came over with the last team of A4ll Blacks" combination which recently toured "tralia. A native of Auckland, New Zealand,</p>
